## Step 3 — host the archive as a new fork release asset

A **new tag** is used rather than replacing the asset on `semantic_joint_ctxmix-afr1`, so any
link already handed out keeps resolving to the bytes it named. If ps1's `-fs1` tag was never
created, `-fs2` is simply the second tag; if it was, `-fs2` is the third and both older links
keep resolving.

```bash
gh release create semantic_joint_ctxmix-fs2 \
    --repo adpena/comma_video_compression_challenge \
    --title "semantic_joint_ctxmix fs2 archive" \
    --notes "archive.zip — SHA-256 a8f3a3791499b2b62ee4d16bc67f15f819f454dc9b88e3cce04fe50a30427bb6, 180023 bytes"

gh release upload semantic_joint_ctxmix-fs2 \
    /Volumes/APDataStore/pact/ddm_ps2_pr140_update_prep/evidence/rebuild/run1_archive.zip#archive.zip \
    --repo adpena/comma_video_compression_challenge
```

The auto-mode classifier blocked the binary upload four times during the PR #140 posting; the
operator's explicit instruction was required then and is required again.

## Step 4 — fetchback verification (MANDATORY before the body is edited)

```bash
cd /Volumes/APDataStore/pact/ddm_ps2_pr140_update_prep/evidence
curl -fL -o fetchback_archive.zip \
  https://github.com/adpena/comma_video_compression_challenge/releases/download/semantic_joint_ctxmix-fs2/archive.zip
shasum -a 256 fetchback_archive.zip
stat -f '%z' fetchback_archive.zip
cmp fetchback_archive.zip rebuild/run1_archive.zip && echo HOSTED_BYTES_IDENTICAL
```

Required result: `a8f3a3791499b2b62ee4d16bc67f15f819f454dc9b88e3cce04fe50a30427bb6`, `180023`,
`HOSTED_BYTES_IDENTICAL`. If any of the three differs, **stop** — do not edit the PR body.

